H — AI Engineering Log:
Prompt:
Act as a Python pair programmer. Implement only the Appointment class from the approved SmartCare UML...

AI Contribution:
- AppointmentStatus enum
- Appointment class with protected status transitions

Decision:
Accepted with minor formatting cleanup.

Reason:
Matches UML, respects domain rules, no invented features.

Verification:
Manual tests confirmed correct transitions and error handling.

Reflection:
The AI generated appointment class was mostly correct, but I still had to check for over design
and hidden assumptions. The biggest issue I watched for was public state mutation, because the domain
model reuqires strict protection of appointment status transitions. The AI followed the prompt and used 
private attributes with controlled methods, which aligned with the UML. I rejected any AI suggestions
involving database logic, notifications, and manger classes because these were outside the domain layer
and not supported by the requirements. The approved design constrained the AI by limiting the scope to 
pure domain behaviour,no SQL, no UL, no external services and no inheritance. This forced the AI to stay
within the boundaries of the Smart care model. The hardest part was ensuring the AI didn't invent new responsibilities,
especially around cancellation logic or sechduling conflicts. The UML clearly defined what appointment
owns, so any behaviour not visible in the diagram had to be removed. The final implementation remained simple,
consitent, and aligned with the domain rules.
